{"kind":"assert","text":"Correction to planner assert 66f8b350, part (1), per the checker: the provider's create takes scope and lifetime only, no label; an inventory cannot identify an ambiguous create by timing, and late application has no completion fence. So the sweep must not infer any id from a window or label, and listing is observation only. The rule is: an unknown ForkTokens record stays unknown until its own create answer arrives or a documented completion fence applies; it is never settled by inventory or time (R-MINT-5). To honour never-revoke-unattributed, the fork sweep (R-WS-3) does not revoke any token on a fork while that fork has an unknown record whose asked lifetime plus the clock allowance has not yet elapsed since the request; after that time any token the create could have made has expired, so sweeping cannot revoke it, and the sweep resumes while the record itself stays unknown. Part (2) stands as the rule but is to be made normative: the lane amends R-MINT-3 so that once an id is received it is written durably before any revoke is attempted, a failed write is retried with the id still in hand, and the existing failed-write clause applies only before an id is known. The repair adopts this corrected reading."}